& [Fault]
  + implementation progress was initially appended to five byte-bound formation artifacts and dual-PowerShell replay refused the resulting design identity against the immutable satisfaction-signature binding

& [Containment]
  + publication verification stopped before an implementation publication claim and before any authority-bearing or live action
  + Git diff isolated every appended block and the historical formation commit remained unchanged and remote-equal

& [Resolution]
  + remove only the new appended blocks restore all five signed formation artifacts exactly to HEAD and retain implementation knowledge in new proof review checkpoint fault attribution and mutable parent-navigation artifacts

& [Lesson]
  + published signed SJS artifacts are historical graph nodes not mutable status pages; later phases must add new nodes and update only explicitly mutable navigation surfaces
